Unknown: Well,

02:32:13.828 --> 02:32:14.888
Delwath: I'll tell her, I mean,

02:32:17.308 --> 02:32:20.348
Delwath: I think it's worth, uh, investigating, right?

02:32:20.348 --> 02:32:22.188
Delwath: If it's more Dunmari, they might have seen something.

02:32:23.528 --> 02:32:24.238
Delwath: If it's beasts,

02:32:25.768 --> 02:32:26.688
Delwath: well, we've found something.

02:32:30.032 --> 02:32:33.752
Seeker: Tim, it's not especially weird that there would be a canyon over in that other direction, is it?

02:32:33.752 --> 02:32:34.952
Seeker: Is that, like, super unnatural?

02:32:37.572 --> 02:32:43.672
DM: Uh, it's hard... I mean, if you could get closer to it, it would be easier for you to tell.

02:32:43.672 --> 02:32:44.432
DM: Um, I think

02:32:45.692 --> 02:32:55.352
DM: given the terrain here, it would certainly be plausible that there was a, a large na- that this sort of canyon lands-y area fed into a large natural canyon.

02:32:55.352 --> 02:32:58.672
DM: Although, you haven't really got the sense that there's enough,

02:32:59.892 --> 02:33:06.962
DM: enough running water. But, you know, it could be, you know, a river could easily be down in the bottom of a canyon to carve it out, and-

02:33:06.962 --> 02:33:07.752
Seeker: Mm-hmm

02:33:07.752 --> 02:33:12.032
DM: ... you know, feeding the oasis or something, and still there not be a lot of green plants here,

02:33:13.332 --> 02:33:15.492
DM: right? It could just be like the Grand Canyon, right?

02:33:15.492 --> 02:33:17.462
DM: Like, there's, it's desert all around.

02:33:17.462 --> 02:33:17.472
Unknown: Yeah.

02:33:17.472 --> 02:33:20.392
DM: But down at the bottom of the canyon there's some water.

02:33:20.392 --> 02:33:20.892
DM: Mm-hmm.

02:33:20.892 --> 02:33:25.912
DM: So it certainly would be plausible based on the terrain you are now, but you'd need to get closer to examine it carefully.

02:33:27.192 --> 02:33:28.812
Seeker: Yeah, let's go check out the, the,

02:33:30.212 --> 02:33:31.852
Seeker: the, uh, action.

02:33:33.592 --> 02:33:33.822
Unknown: Okay.

02:33:35.011 --> 02:33:37.112
DM: So it looks like y- it's probably, you know,

02:33:38.792 --> 02:33:46.052
DM: if you angle your dir- you could make a guesses to angle your direction of travel, so you would kind of cut off the whatever's moving up there.

02:33:46.052 --> 02:33:47.532
DM: But it's not that far away.

02:33:47.532 --> 02:33:49.992
DM: It's like an hour or two travel at most.

02:33:51.172 --> 02:33:53.712
Wellby: Okay. Let's do it.

02:33:53.712 --> 02:33:53.892
Unknown: Okay.

02:33:55.132 --> 02:34:01.792
DM: Um, so you head sort of, now you're kind of heading northwest actually, um, because of the direction of travel of this, um,

02:34:03.552 --> 02:34:12.792
DM: o- of this dust cloud, and kind of get back out of the canyon lands and, um, sort of head across the scrub desert.

02:34:13.952 --> 02:34:14.232
Unknown: And

02:34:15.812 --> 02:34:25.852
DM: as you get, as you get closer, um, you can, you can see when you're, um, not too far off that, um, this is

02:34:25.852 --> 02:34:29.052
DM: a, it's definitely a Dunmarion horseback.

02:34:29.052 --> 02:34:31.772
DM: Um, it's a

02:34:33.112 --> 02:34:40.572
DM: younger woman riding at a medium trot who kind of notices you coming and, um, pulls up,

02:34:41.652 --> 02:34:46.832
DM: and kind of looks at you a bit strangely, s- keeping her distance, and, um,

02:34:48.292 --> 02:34:50.912
DM: and h- and sort of hails you in Dunmari.

02:34:52.752 --> 02:34:53.872
DM: "Ho, travelers."

02:34:55.092 --> 02:34:57.082
Delwath: Again, staying far away.

02:34:57.082 --> 02:35:05.952
Delwath: I'll, I'll respond back, um, also in Dunmari, greeting her and telling her we, um, we've set out from...

02:35:08.252 --> 02:35:10.732
Delwath: I'm blanking on the name. Kara- Karawa?

02:35:10.732 --> 02:35:11.132
Unknown: Karawa.

02:35:11.132 --> 02:35:12.222
Kenzo: Yep. Karawa.

02:35:12.222 --> 02:35:12.312
Unknown: Karawa.

02:35:12.312 --> 02:35:12.592
Unknown: Um,

02:35:13.672 --> 02:35:15.412
Delwath: we've set out from Karawa, um,

02:35:17.072 --> 02:35:21.092
Delwath: uh, in the last few hours, tracking some strange beasts.

02:35:23.492 --> 02:35:23.572
Unknown: Um-

02:35:23.572 --> 02:35:24.492
Delwath: Have you seen anything-

02:35:25.552 --> 02:35:25.741
Unknown: Sh- she, like-

02:35:25.741 --> 02:35:27.092
Delwath: ... out on the plains?

02:35:27.092 --> 02:35:29.032
DM: ... looks at you all, and,

02:35:30.312 --> 02:35:37.752
DM: you know, kind of a little bit taken aback by this sight, and stares at you in particular, um, Delwath.

02:35:37.752 --> 02:35:38.142
Unknown: And then,

02:35:39.332 --> 02:35:46.232
DM: uh, kind of thinks for a minute, and realization dawns on her and she says, "The elf.

02:35:46.232 --> 02:35:47.352
DM: You must be the elf.

02:35:48.772 --> 02:35:49.622
Delwath: Greetings."

02:35:49.622 --> 02:35:50.112
Delwath: I nod slightly.

02:35:52.112 --> 02:35:53.252
DM: "My name is Alesh.

02:35:54.532 --> 02:35:54.732
Unknown: Uh,

02:35:56.632 --> 02:35:57.162
Delwath: it is,

02:35:58.692 --> 02:36:02.132
DM: um, it is unexpected to meet you out here.

02:36:02.132 --> 02:36:02.332
Unknown: Uh,

02:36:04.272 --> 02:36:05.802
DM: but interesting that you've

02:36:06.972 --> 02:36:09.392
DM: reported strange beasts.

02:36:09.392 --> 02:36:10.872
DM: Um, I am a, I'm a scout.

02:36:10.872 --> 02:36:12.992
DM: I've been, uh, riding ahead.

02:36:12.992 --> 02:36:15.122
DM: I'm returning from, um,

02:36:16.492 --> 02:36:21.432
DM: investigating the area around the, the Gomat Oasis.

02:36:21.432 --> 02:36:25.812
DM: Uh, there's been reports of people going missing, of herders and shepherds.

02:36:25.812 --> 02:36:26.792
DM: And, um,

02:36:28.892 --> 02:36:30.412
DM: I, I am concerned.

02:36:32.032 --> 02:36:40.772
DM: There's strange rumors traveling among the scouts and pastoralists that are, um, you know, that wander in these lands.

02:36:40.772 --> 02:36:42.292
DM: And despite the

02:36:43.672 --> 02:36:52.742
DM: good quality of the grazing over there, um, you know, my family's been quite skeptical of, of heading in that direction without, uh,

02:36:55.232 --> 02:37:03.172
DM: investigating. But I was just d- I was, I'm just riding, riding back from the Gomat Oasis itself, and have not seen anything the past day along the road.

02:37:04.472 --> 02:37:04.492
Unknown: How-

02:37:04.492 --> 02:37:06.112
DM: Where did you say you saw these animals?

02:37:08.872 --> 02:37:12.872
Delwath: Uh, two, two hyenas the size of small horses.

02:37:12.872 --> 02:37:14.672
Delwath: That's about right, right?

02:37:14.672 --> 02:37:15.032
Unknown: Um-

02:37:15.032 --> 02:37:15.932
DM: Uh, yeah

02:37:15.932 --> 02:37:18.262
Kenzo: ... uh, were,

02:37:19.372 --> 02:37:23.512
Delwath: uh, rampaging in Karawa, Karawa at dawn this morning.

02:37:25.532 --> 02:37:27.792
DM: Um, she looks, she looks kind of, uh,

02:37:29.572 --> 02:37:33.352
DM: um, shocked when you say that, and she, and, like, the blood drains from her face and she says,

02:37:34.712 --> 02:37:37.232
DM: "Were people killed? I, I have family there.

02:37:37.232 --> 02:37:38.092
DM: I have friends."

02:37:39.212 --> 02:37:40.122
Delwath: No. M-

02:37:41.952 --> 02:37:45.862
Delwath: One, one man was badly injured, but, um, he's under the care of the,

02:37:46.912 --> 02:37:48.302
Delwath: of the Shakun now,

02:37:49.432 --> 02:37:51.272
Delwath: and I believe will make a full recovery.

02:37:53.512 --> 02:37:55.672
DM: Um, she, she kind of, um,

02:37:56.872 --> 02:37:58.872
DM: relaxes a little bit and says...

02:37:58.872 --> 02:38:09.012
DM: And, and she's now, she's sort of, um, inched closer to you as you've been talking, and moved, you know, from a, a, a stance of basically being ready to gallop away any second

02:38:09.012 --> 02:38:09.432
Unknown: to, uh,

02:38:10.752 --> 02:38:12.571
DM: um, to just kind of talking normally.

02:38:12.572 --> 02:38:14.312
DM: Although, she's, she hasn't dismounted.

02:38:14.312 --> 02:38:16.232
DM: She's still on her horse.

02:38:16.232 --> 02:38:16.472
Unknown: Um,

02:38:18.432 --> 02:38:24.312
DM: and sh- and she says, "And you're, you know, you're out here hunting the, these beasts?

02:38:24.312 --> 02:38:27.032
DM: Do you, do you suspect there's more of them?

02:38:27.032 --> 02:38:28.212
DM: Should w- should I be worried?"

02:38:30.332 --> 02:38:32.492
Delwath: I think from of all you've just told us, yes.

02:38:37.016 --> 02:38:39.056
DM: She kind of sighs a little bit and says,

02:38:40.176 --> 02:38:40.716
DM: "It seemed,

02:38:42.376 --> 02:38:45.296
DM: it seemed like maybe the danger was past.

02:38:45.296 --> 02:38:46.936
DM: I had heard rumors, but I,

02:38:48.046 --> 02:38:50.635
DM: I travel these roads quite frequently.

02:38:50.636 --> 02:38:51.866
DM: There's..."

02:38:51.866 --> 02:38:57.236
DM: Um, and her eyes light up a little and she says, "There's lots of old battle sites along these roads, and

02:38:58.396 --> 02:39:01.216
DM: things to find, spears, arrows,

02:39:02.236 --> 02:39:03.596
DM: shields sometimes.

02:39:05.156 --> 02:39:05.356
Unknown: Uh,

02:39:06.576 --> 02:39:07.206
DM: and although

02:39:08.536 --> 02:39:12.476
DM: years ago in my childhood people would say, 'Oh, it's too dangerous,'

02:39:13.876 --> 02:39:23.976
DM: um, it's, it's felt safer recently, and, and I've been on the r- I've been tr- ranging wide with my family over the

02:39:23.976 --> 02:39:26.236
DM: past six months, and I did not realize

02:39:27.756 --> 02:39:30.156
DM: the danger had, I guess, has returned."

02:39:32.136 --> 02:39:33.376
Kenzo: What do you mean by has returned?

02:39:36.396 --> 02:39:40.716
DM: Well, the, you know, the, people when, when I was a kid,

02:39:41.855 --> 02:39:44.736
DM: when I was growing up 15, 20 years ago,

02:39:46.336 --> 02:39:51.256
DM: people would go missing. We never, we never went into the, into the, um...

02:39:54.116 --> 02:39:54.996
DM: Oops, sorry, hold on.

02:39:56.036 --> 02:39:59.116
DM: We never went into the Nashtkar, the Blasted Plains.

02:40:00.296 --> 02:40:05.736
DM: You know, as a, as a kid who tr- who traveled around here, I was, you know, you know there's a lot of history.

02:40:05.736 --> 02:40:09.836
DM: And she, and she looks sort of specifically at...

02:40:09.836 --> 02:40:18.156
DM: Well, she kind of looks at all of you, like, kind of questioning, you know, are, are these people interested in history?

02:40:18.156 --> 02:40:18.416
Unknown: Um,

02:40:19.716 --> 02:40:24.816
DM: and then looks at, at Kenzo, who is, uh, who is Dunmari.

02:40:24.816 --> 02:40:26.716
DM: Um, who do I need to message?

02:40:26.716 --> 02:40:26.796
Unknown: Uh.

02:40:27.846 --> 02:40:35.856
Unknown: [coughs]

02:40:37.336 --> 02:40:43.416
Kenzo: Do, do, uh, do Seeker and, um, uh, Wellby understand Dunmari?

02:40:44.756 --> 02:40:46.706
DM: Yeah, everybody understands Dunmari.

02:40:46.706 --> 02:40:51.736
DM: I just gave you all Dunmari 'cause it would be frustrating and annoying for n- you not to.

02:40:51.736 --> 02:40:52.796
Kenzo: [laughs] Yeah.

02:40:52.796 --> 02:40:53.036
Unknown: Um,

02:40:54.636 --> 02:40:56.116
DM: yeah, so everybody understands Dunmari.

02:40:56.116 --> 02:41:01.856
DM: I mean, Wellby's been traveling long enough and, and Seeker, you've both been traveling enough to have picked it up.

02:41:01.856 --> 02:41:03.216
DM: And, um,

02:41:06.196 --> 02:41:08.426
DM: uh, and she says, "So, you know, my,

02:41:09.716 --> 02:41:12.056
DM: the, the history here is, is fascinating.

02:41:12.056 --> 02:41:13.716
DM: I don't know how much you know about, well..."

02:41:13.716 --> 02:41:20.616
DM: And then she kind of stops herself and, and looks at, um, looks at Delwath and says, "I guess the elf would know the most,

02:41:21.816 --> 02:41:23.376
DM: more than me.

02:41:23.376 --> 02:41:23.445
Unknown: Um,

02:41:25.196 --> 02:41:26.676
DM: people say that you're very old."

02:41:28.105 --> 02:41:29.596
Delwath: Delwath just kind of nods a bit.

02:41:31.376 --> 02:41:32.936
DM: And, and then she says, um,

02:41:35.796 --> 02:41:37.636
DM: "You know, but the, the

02:41:38.936 --> 02:41:45.536
DM: history is so fascinating, and I, I was always told, 'Oh, don't go digging around those old graves.

02:41:45.536 --> 02:41:47.636
DM: You don't know what you might find.

02:41:47.636 --> 02:41:49.756
DM: Those battle sites are...

02:41:49.756 --> 02:41:51.696
DM: Who knows what, what could still be there.'

02:41:53.896 --> 02:42:04.216
DM: But it, but in the past few years, it's felt safer, and people have been grazing as far, actually east of, of Gomat, um, as far as the canyon even.

02:42:04.216 --> 02:42:04.616
Unknown: Uh,

02:42:06.676 --> 02:42:14.616
DM: but if what you said is true and danger is coming out of the east again, I fear that, that, um, you know, maybe those days of my childhood are coming back.

02:42:16.036 --> 02:42:17.976
Wellby: There's a few..."

02:42:17.976 --> 02:42:19.196
DM: Sorry, go ahead.

02:42:19.196 --> 02:42:26.496
Wellby: Is there a path from the Gomat Oasis to the canyon that doesn't pass through the Badlands?

02:42:26.496 --> 02:42:28.616
DM: Yeah, just follow the road east.

02:42:28.616 --> 02:42:38.716
DM: You're now... I mean, you're on this ancient, this sort of old trade road where you can see occasionally, like, um, it's mostly just a track kind

02:42:38.716 --> 02:42:48.896
DM: of kicked up through the, you know, s- through the sand, but every now and then there's, like, a paving stone or a, um, you know, kind of a, a little bit of ancient history

02:42:48.896 --> 02:42:50.216
DM: suggesting that it's, um,

02:42:52.116 --> 02:42:53.256
DM: uh, you know, uh...

02:42:56.766 --> 02:43:00.596
DM: Uh, you can sort of, you can sense, you can sort of see the history of the road.

02:43:00.596 --> 02:43:05.036
DM: Like, you can tell that this used to be, many, many years ago, well-traveled.

02:43:05.036 --> 02:43:13.016
DM: It's just been worn down and broken up, and the, and the paving stones have all cracked and everything, but there's definitely a road you can follow.

02:43:13.016 --> 02:43:22.315
DM: So the road'll take you straight to Gomat, and, and from there, um, there's not a, there's not a way across the canyon that I know of.

02:43:22.316 --> 02:43:23.816
DM: The road sort of ends.

02:43:25.316 --> 02:43:28.756
DM: But certainly it'll take you to the canyon.

02:43:28.756 --> 02:43:30.376
DM: I've been as far as that before.

02:43:30.376 --> 02:43:32.836
DM: In fact, there was a, just, um,

02:43:35.316 --> 02:43:45.856
DM: just last night, I, I spent the night with a, a couple of, um, herding families and their flocks of sheep, uh, around Gomat,

02:43:45.856 --> 02:43:47.096
DM: uh, and,

02:43:48.156 --> 02:43:52.276
DM: and I, uh, uh, just came straight on the road this morning.

02:43:52.276 --> 02:43:53.076
DM: It's, it's,

02:43:55.016 --> 02:44:00.416
DM: you know, no more than a, a day's walk to the, to the oasis.

02:44:00.416 --> 02:44:02.516
DM: Maybe two, depending on how fast you walk.

02:44:03.656 --> 02:44:03.916
Unknown: Um,

02:44:05.496 --> 02:44:07.296
DM: eight hours on, on a fast horse.

02:44:09.156 --> 02:44:11.696
DM: But it'll take you straight through the, the canyon lands.

02:44:11.696 --> 02:44:14.856
DM: I, I wouldn't wander south of here much.

02:44:14.856 --> 02:44:16.066
DM: It's trackless there.

02:44:16.066 --> 02:44:17.996
DM: It's... Sometimes even I get lost.

02:44:19.696 --> 02:44:20.326
DM: Hm. Mm-hmm.

02:44:22.316 --> 02:44:25.315
Kenzo: Well, we seek the origins of these strange hyenas.

02:44:25.316 --> 02:44:26.276
Kenzo: It's, uh,

02:44:28.036 --> 02:44:31.436
Kenzo: unclear if you've seen anything related to their origin.

02:44:31.436 --> 02:44:34.055
Kenzo: Sounds like you may not have.

02:44:34.056 --> 02:44:39.536
DM: I haven't seen anything related to those, but strange beasts, I always say, must be the Blasted Lands.

02:44:40.636 --> 02:44:42.716
Wellby: Would there be anyone...

02:44:42.716 --> 02:44:44.196
Wellby: Oh, go ahead, sorry.

02:44:44.196 --> 02:44:45.476
DM: Who knows what comes out of there?

02:44:46.596 --> 02:44:56.756
Wellby: Hmm. Beside the Gomat Oasis and the road east toward the canyon from there, are there any families or herders

02:44:56.756 --> 02:45:01.496
Wellby: or anyone east or east by northeast of here?

02:45:03.236 --> 02:45:04.675
Wellby: No one goes-

02:45:04.676 --> 02:45:07.556
Wellby: When the creature, when the creature came into town and had blood on it, that it

02:45:09.136 --> 02:45:10.456
Wellby: must have come from somewhere.

02:45:13.916 --> 02:45:14.596
DM: She looks,

02:45:16.156 --> 02:45:19.456
DM: um, a little bit pale when you say that, and she says,

02:45:21.236 --> 02:45:24.196
DM: "A straight line

02:45:25.616 --> 02:45:31.816
DM: from Gomat to Karawa would pass through the edge of those canyon lands."

02:45:34.716 --> 02:45:36.276
Wellby: I think we should push to the oasis.

02:45:37.946 --> 02:45:40.536
DM: There were defi- there's definitely, you know,

02:45:42.116 --> 02:45:46.976
DM: people coming in, gathering at Gomat and heading into Karawa for the,

02:45:48.216 --> 02:45:49.116
DM: for the, um,

02:45:52.396 --> 02:45:56.176
DM: for the festival. Uh, you said they attacked this morning?

02:45:58.276 --> 02:45:58.286
Unknown: Yeah.

02:45:58.286 --> 02:46:01.246
DM: She kind of breathes a sigh of relief in, uh, when you say that, and she says,

02:46:02.306 --> 02:46:08.116
DM: "They couldn't have traveled from Gomat to town in only a few hours,

02:46:09.516 --> 02:46:13.336
DM: less than an hour. The f- the families that left this morning must be safe.

02:46:16.176 --> 02:46:16.376
Unknown: But

02:46:17.536 --> 02:46:18.536
DM: others around here,

02:46:21.236 --> 02:46:23.316
DM: you do make, you do make me nervous."

02:46:25.756 --> 02:46:25.856
Unknown: Hmm.

02:46:27.276 --> 02:46:28.676
Kenzo: I glance at the, the company.

02:46:29.856 --> 02:46:30.776
Kenzo: Where do you think we should go?

02:46:36.356 --> 02:46:38.276
Wellby: I think we should push to the oasis.

02:46:38.276 --> 02:46:45.796
Wellby: If there's anyone who would have been out in this land, you know, to the east or to the northeast of here,

02:46:47.476 --> 02:46:52.556
Wellby: presumably some word of that would have come to the people gathering at the oasis.

02:46:52.556 --> 02:46:54.685
Wellby: I, I feel like that's our best bet-

02:46:54.685 --> 02:46:54.685
Unknown: Yeah

02:46:54.685 --> 02:46:55.315
Delwath: ... to learn more.

02:46:57.586 --> 02:46:57.956
Unknown: Mm-hmm.

02:46:59.176 --> 02:47:03.816
Kenzo: How far, uh, how far is it from here to the oasis, based on what she was saying?

02:47:03.816 --> 02:47:06.196
DM: So, I mean, she rode

02:47:07.456 --> 02:47:11.356
DM: eight hours at a fast, fast pace.

02:47:11.356 --> 02:47:12.396
DM: I think on foot,

02:47:13.656 --> 02:47:18.376
DM: you know, traveling in relatively unfamiliar terrain, it would take you

02:47:19.516 --> 02:47:20.356
DM: a day or two.

02:47:22.236 --> 02:47:22.556
Unknown: Not-

02:47:22.556 --> 02:47:24.626
DM: When is the festival?

02:47:24.626 --> 02:47:25.896
DM: Festival's in like two weeks.

02:47:27.685 --> 02:47:28.046
Unknown: Hmm.

02:47:29.176 --> 02:47:30.916
Kenzo: It's, this is a bit far to stray,

02:47:32.316 --> 02:47:33.836
Kenzo: given the time of the festival.

02:47:33.836 --> 02:47:36.046
Wellby: Oh, sorry. Could we get there like by tomorrow night?

02:47:38.236 --> 02:47:39.846
DM: You could, you could be at the...

02:47:39.846 --> 02:47:40.056
Unknown: Eh,

02:47:41.376 --> 02:47:43.976
DM: well, it's already like 4:00 in the afternoon by now.

02:47:45.396 --> 02:47:49.756
DM: Um, you could get a few more hours tonight, um, travel all day.

02:47:50.796 --> 02:47:52.536
DM: You probably wouldn't quite get there.

02:47:52.536 --> 02:47:56.676
DM: Un- if you could push on into the night, you could get there past dark, for sure,

02:47:58.096 --> 02:47:59.896
DM: if you made a long day of it tomorrow.

02:48:03.096 --> 02:48:04.016
DM: But it would be dark.

02:48:05.716 --> 02:48:06.096
Unknown: Um...

02:48:14.936 --> 02:48:15.856
Kenzo: What do you say, travelers?

02:48:18.056 --> 02:48:19.916
