02:48:19.916 --> 02:48:20.896
DM: I see it. Um,

02:48:22.136 --> 02:48:23.556
DM: sorry, I missed the earlier one.

02:48:23.556 --> 02:48:25.196
Delwath: No, that one doesn't matter as much, but-

02:48:25.196 --> 02:48:25.636
Unknown: Okay.

02:48:25.636 --> 02:48:26.756
Kenzo: Tim, you saw the thing I sent you, right?

02:48:28.476 --> 02:48:30.296
DM: Um, um, yes.

02:48:31.376 --> 02:48:31.856
Kenzo: Okay.

02:48:31.856 --> 02:48:32.216
Unknown: I did.

02:48:33.396 --> 02:48:34.376
DM: Okay. Uh...

02:48:37.516 --> 02:48:38.776
Kenzo: What say you, travelers?

02:48:38.776 --> 02:48:39.236
DM: Sh- should we

02:48:40.296 --> 02:48:41.616
Kenzo: continue onward to the oasis?

02:48:44.236 --> 02:48:46.496
Seeker: Seems like the only reasonable course.

02:48:50.176 --> 02:48:52.656
Kenzo: I worry about straying too far from town, but

02:48:54.336 --> 02:48:56.396
Kenzo: I think if we, uh, investigate further there and...

02:48:57.876 --> 02:49:00.056
Delwath: And, and how sure are we that

02:49:01.196 --> 02:49:02.776
Delwath: nothing will come from another direction?

02:49:04.935 --> 02:49:07.016
Wellby: Tell us about the last two attacks.

02:49:07.016 --> 02:49:10.696
Wellby: Do you know where those came from or how far spaced they were?

02:49:10.696 --> 02:49:11.496
Seeker: I was wondering about that.

02:49:13.276 --> 02:49:13.476
Unknown: Uh...

02:49:18.056 --> 02:49:19.066
Delwath: Tim, did you hear the question?

02:49:20.536 --> 02:49:22.436
DM: Um, how far spaced are the attacks?

02:49:22.436 --> 02:49:23.326
DM: Yeah. I, I don't know-

02:49:23.326 --> 02:49:26.996
DM: Uh, they both happened, they both happened within the past two weeks.

02:49:28.556 --> 02:49:28.806
Unknown: But they were like-

02:49:28.806 --> 02:49:29.316
Delwath: But the previous-

02:49:31.376 --> 02:49:32.976
DM: The first one was two weeks ago,

02:49:34.316 --> 02:49:40.336
DM: and the next one was about six days after that, and then nothing for

02:49:41.456 --> 02:49:43.756
DM: eight or nine, eight days, roughly.

02:49:43.756 --> 02:49:51.436
Delwath: Hmm. But the previous attacks, the previous attacks were just, we all thought they were just wild, wild creatures.

02:49:51.436 --> 02:49:53.216
Delwath: They were not these oversized beasts.

02:49:54.776 --> 02:49:55.896
Wellby: Hmm.

02:49:58.216 --> 02:50:03.196
Kenzo: Perhaps should we head back to town then in case, uh, another, another attack strikes again?

02:50:03.196 --> 02:50:04.796
Kenzo: Without us, is the town defenseless?

02:50:07.456 --> 02:50:08.916
Kenzo: I'm glancing at the company.

02:50:08.916 --> 02:50:10.776
Delwath: It, it's not defenseless, but

02:50:13.116 --> 02:50:15.476
Delwath: it's definitely not well defended either.

02:50:16.516 --> 02:50:16.636
Unknown: Hmm.

02:50:17.876 --> 02:50:22.916
Wellby: If we stay in town to defend it, though, there's no way for us to know the source or to try and track it.

02:50:24.356 --> 02:50:24.496
Unknown: Hmm.

02:50:26.476 --> 02:50:36.176
Kenzo: Well, if we, if we make haste to the oasis, learn what, learn what we can there, uh, we can be back in, back to town in, what, two days, three days?

02:50:38.116 --> 02:50:48.156
DM: If you push yourselves, yeah, you could be, if you, you could make it to the oasis by tomorrow night, and then it would take you a, a, you know, a day and a half, again,

02:50:48.156 --> 02:50:51.376
DM: pushing yourself long, hard days to get back to town.

02:50:53.648 --> 02:50:55.588
Kenzo: I'm new to the town. I, I'm new to Karawa.

02:50:55.588 --> 02:50:59.988
Kenzo: I'm not, not familiar with its denizens or, or its defenses.

02:50:59.988 --> 02:51:01.758
Kenzo: If you, if you feel like,

02:51:02.788 --> 02:51:06.268
Kenzo: uh, our, our, uh, our absence

02:51:07.528 --> 02:51:10.808
Kenzo: and our, our ability to learn more will, will be e- more useful,

02:51:12.148 --> 02:51:13.948
Kenzo: I defer to, to you all who've been there longer.

02:51:16.028 --> 02:51:16.368
Unknown: I think

02:51:17.608 --> 02:51:20.688
Delwath: we should go to the oasis, but with haste.

02:51:23.808 --> 02:51:24.328
Kenzo: All right then.

02:51:25.788 --> 02:51:30.307
Kenzo: Um, I, I glance over at the Dunmari, uh, uh, horse rider.

02:51:30.308 --> 02:51:30.508
Unknown: Um,

02:51:32.108 --> 02:51:33.708
Kenzo: "Friend, what's your name?

02:51:33.708 --> 02:51:36.368
Kenzo: I'm Kenzo. Also, also D- also Dunmari.

02:51:36.368 --> 02:51:37.847
Kenzo: It's good to seem, see you here."

02:51:39.488 --> 02:51:42.308
DM: Uh, her, her name is Alesh.

02:51:42.308 --> 02:51:42.748
Unknown: Alesh.

02:51:43.988 --> 02:51:44.487
Kenzo: Alesh,

02:51:45.628 --> 02:51:48.628
Kenzo: my companions and I, I think we're gonna head to the oasis.

02:51:48.628 --> 02:51:50.108
Kenzo: Are you safe here?

02:51:50.108 --> 02:51:51.168
DM: You should be, you should be

02:51:52.288 --> 02:51:55.048
Kenzo: careful. These are, these are dangerous times.

02:51:56.348 --> 02:51:59.248
DM: I'm fast. There's few things that can catch me on my horse.

02:52:00.428 --> 02:52:02.288
DM: She has, like, a pretty confident look.

02:52:02.288 --> 02:52:05.188
DM: I mean, she was, you know, she looks-

02:52:05.188 --> 02:52:05.408
Unknown: Yeah

02:52:05.408 --> 02:52:07.768
DM: ... comf- very comfortable on horseback.

02:52:07.768 --> 02:52:07.818
Unknown: Um,

02:52:09.008 --> 02:52:11.288
DM: and she says, "And I need to get back to my family anyway.

02:52:11.288 --> 02:52:18.668
DM: They've been, we've been, uh, looking for more pasture land that seems safe, and I'm not gonna take them east after hearing these stories.

02:52:18.668 --> 02:52:26.048
DM: I think we're gonna head north for, for a bit more grazing and fatten up our, our animals before taking them into town for the festival."

02:52:27.068 --> 02:52:27.948
Kenzo: Hm. Good.

02:52:30.788 --> 02:52:32.388
Kenzo: Well then, safe travels.

02:52:32.388 --> 02:52:34.228
Kenzo: Uh, please, please be safe.

02:52:34.228 --> 02:52:34.888
DM: And

02:52:36.688 --> 02:52:37.098
Unknown: if we-

02:52:37.098 --> 02:52:37.228
Unknown: Um

02:52:37.228 --> 02:52:39.098
Kenzo: ... we hear word in the oasis, uh, we'll...

02:52:39.098 --> 02:52:39.328
Unknown: Actually,

02:52:40.568 --> 02:52:43.828
Kenzo: are you, do you have friends in the oasis that you might recommend we speak with to learn more?

02:52:46.428 --> 02:52:50.768
DM: Uh, uh, there was a f- there was a few, uh, uh, folks that I,

02:52:52.188 --> 02:52:53.608
DM: I spent the night with.

02:52:53.608 --> 02:52:59.468
DM: Um, they seemed, they seemed welcoming, and we traded stories.

02:52:59.468 --> 02:53:04.088
DM: Uh, if you are, if you are looking for anybody, there's not a...

02:53:04.088 --> 02:53:06.268
DM: There's, just to be clear, there's not a town there.

02:53:06.268 --> 02:53:09.188
DM: It's like, it's, it's not a built-up oasis like Karawa.

02:53:09.188 --> 02:53:13.748
DM: It's just a sort of a place where, where people set up camp for a week-

02:53:13.748 --> 02:53:13.758
Unknown: Mm-hmm

02:53:13.758 --> 02:53:16.168
DM: ... when they're grazing their animals and stuff.

02:53:16.168 --> 02:53:16.648
DM: Um-

02:53:16.648 --> 02:53:18.728
Kenzo: Oh, so it's not, like, permanent dwellings.

02:53:18.728 --> 02:53:29.388
DM: It's not permanent dwellings, but, but, um, uh, when I was there, um, yeah, ask for, um, ask for Akan and his family.

02:53:29.388 --> 02:53:35.427
DM: Um, they were camped there last night and were planning on spending a few more days, uh, grazing their herds there.

02:53:38.188 --> 02:53:43.888
DM: Uh, and they seemed friendly and, and, and, uh, we shared some good stories.

02:53:45.488 --> 02:53:46.728
Kenzo: Perfect. We'll seek them.

02:53:47.848 --> 02:53:55.248
DM: Um, and as she's, she goes to ride off, uh, "I must," she says, "I must hurry," and then goes to ride off and then says, "And if you find any,

02:53:56.928 --> 02:54:03.828
DM: any battle sites or any relics of ancient Dunmore, Dunmar, I'll be at the festival.

02:54:03.828 --> 02:54:05.848
DM: Come find me. I'd be curious to know."

02:54:08.208 --> 02:54:08.368
Unknown: Hm.

02:54:10.248 --> 02:54:15.728
DM: And with that, she calls over her shoulder, "Stay safe," as she gallops off, um, down the road again.

02:54:15.728 --> 02:54:18.568
Kenzo: Is there, is there, like, a Dunmari greeting or a farewell?

02:54:18.568 --> 02:54:19.868
DM: Um, yeah, uh-

02:54:19.868 --> 02:54:21.788
Kenzo: Whatever it is, I do. Whatever it is, I do it.

02:54:21.788 --> 02:54:22.228
Unknown: Right.

02:54:25.248 --> 02:54:25.668
Unknown: Um,

02:54:27.128 --> 02:54:29.108
DM: how much longer do you guys wanna keep going, by the way?

02:54:32.108 --> 02:54:32.468
Unknown: Mm.

02:54:32.468 --> 02:54:33.588
DM: Should we wrap up and, like-

02:54:35.508 --> 02:54:35.748
Unknown: I'm-

02:54:35.748 --> 02:54:36.698
DM: ... you know, the next-

02:54:36.698 --> 02:54:37.648
DM: ... pretty tired

02:54:37.648 --> 02:54:40.608
DM: ... or, like, keep going a bit past that?

02:54:42.888 --> 02:54:45.708
Kenzo: I think we could... I mean, this is a pretty good spot in a way.

02:54:45.708 --> 02:54:45.948
Unknown: Like, we-

02:54:45.948 --> 02:54:46.017
Unknown: Yeah

02:54:46.017 --> 02:54:47.428
Kenzo: ... could start up at the oasis.

02:54:47.428 --> 02:54:48.028
Wellby: You know, like we-

02:54:48.028 --> 02:54:48.038
Unknown: I think so, yeah

02:54:48.038 --> 02:54:49.218
Kenzo: ... we arrive at the oasis.

02:54:49.218 --> 02:54:50.548
DM: Yeah. Yeah, that's what I was thinking.

02:54:50.548 --> 02:54:50.848
Unknown: That's-

02:54:50.848 --> 02:54:51.017
Unknown: Yeah

02:54:51.017 --> 02:54:53.768
DM: ... let's, that's, like, five or 10 minutes.

02:54:53.768 --> 02:54:53.928
Unknown: Yeah.

02:54:55.108 --> 02:54:56.848
DM: Cool. Okay.

02:54:56.848 --> 02:54:57.108
Unknown: So,

02:54:58.628 --> 02:54:59.598
DM: um, you set out,

02:55:02.648 --> 02:55:06.288
DM: uh, heading towards the oasis, following the road.

02:55:08.028 --> 02:55:09.768
DM: As you,

02:55:11.528 --> 02:55:16.308
DM: as you travel, you can s- you get a sense of the, the sort of history of this place and how

02:55:17.388 --> 02:55:27.488
DM: violent the cataclysms were that, that shook this land, as every now and then you'll see, you know, a stretch of, of, you know, stone tile that's not

02:55:27.488 --> 02:55:35.268
DM: cracked, but a large stone paver that's just tilted straight upright, sitting vertical in the sand.

02:55:35.268 --> 02:55:45.668
DM: And as you pass through this, um, this land, it's easy to follow the, the road, and when you come to the, um, to sort of the edge of the canyon lands, the road

02:55:45.728 --> 02:55:46.608
DM: cuts straight,

02:55:48.348 --> 02:55:51.088
DM: and it seems like it's been cleared, but more recently.

02:55:51.088 --> 02:55:52.108
DM: This is not, um,

02:55:53.188 --> 02:56:00.408
DM: this is not ancient. The canyon lands almost grew up around the road instead of the road being built through them.

02:56:00.408 --> 02:56:10.608
DM: But there's places where, um, you know, dirt, sand and dirt and, and stone has been kind of pushed aside to make a path that at least a horse can travel single file

02:56:10.608 --> 02:56:18.148
DM: through. Um, and this definitely is a, is a, um, a path that gets some, some traffic.

02:56:19.888 --> 02:56:25.848
DM: You spend a cold, quiet night, um, sheltered off the road,

02:56:27.068 --> 02:56:35.808
DM: long resting so you all get your spell slots back and everything, and your, get your charges back for your, the thing we were talking about earlier, Eric.

02:56:37.028 --> 02:56:37.188
Unknown: Cool.

02:56:37.188 --> 02:56:37.368
Unknown: Um,

02:56:39.428 --> 02:56:49.488
DM: get up very early, pre-dawn the following day to, for, to press on, um, traveling as hard and fast as you can to get to

02:56:49.488 --> 02:56:50.268
Delwath: the oasis.

02:56:52.908 --> 02:56:57.008
DM: It's a long day, traveling in the heat of the sun.

02:56:57.008 --> 02:56:58.376
DM: Um- ...

02:56:58.376 --> 02:57:03.416
DM: pushing on, uh, into the, the moonlight evening.

02:57:03.416 --> 02:57:05.506
DM: Um, can you all make constitution checks?

02:57:07.056 --> 02:57:08.435
Kenzo: What?

02:57:09.676 --> 02:57:11.236
Unknown: [laughs]

02:57:11.236 --> 02:57:12.316
Kenzo: Why would we do that, Tim?

02:57:19.836 --> 02:57:20.416
Kenzo: Damn it.

02:57:20.416 --> 02:57:23.196
Wellby: [laughs] That's some good numbers.

02:57:23.196 --> 02:57:24.135
DM: That's awesome.

02:57:24.136 --> 02:57:24.546
Unknown: Oh.

02:57:24.546 --> 02:57:25.136
DM: Oh, shit.

02:57:25.136 --> 02:57:26.436
DM: Oh, no.

02:57:26.436 --> 02:57:26.996
Seeker: Oh, no.

02:57:28.936 --> 02:57:30.016
Seeker: Delwath is fine.

02:57:31.376 --> 02:57:32.476
Seeker: Uh, yeah.

02:57:32.476 --> 02:57:34.236
Wellby: Can all three of us ride on the horse?

02:57:35.456 --> 02:57:36.036
Unknown: [laughs]

02:57:36.036 --> 02:57:44.176
DM: Well, no, one of you can ride on the horse, 'cause the horse is carrying, like, you know, all of your water and, you know, you're in the desert, right?

02:57:44.176 --> 02:57:47.076
DM: You gotta travel with food and water and stuff like that.

02:57:47.076 --> 02:57:47.276
Unknown: Um,

02:57:49.236 --> 02:57:49.556
Unknown: so

02:57:51.296 --> 02:57:52.196
DM: in the moonlight,

02:57:53.536 --> 02:57:56.636
DM: like, the heat of the day just beats down on you.

02:57:57.696 --> 02:58:01.376
DM: The pushing yourself, exerting yourself in the desert, um,

02:58:02.616 --> 02:58:13.136
DM: even those of you who are, who are used to traveling in these conditions, you are, you are pushing yourself, um, harder and, and further to get to this oasis

02:58:13.136 --> 02:58:15.055
DM: as fast as you can.

02:58:15.056 --> 02:58:17.176
DM: And, um,

02:58:19.056 --> 02:58:27.616
DM: Wellby, Seeker, and Kenzo suffer one level of exhaustion from exerting yourself through the day.

02:58:29.896 --> 02:58:31.616
Seeker: Um, how does that work?

02:58:31.616 --> 02:58:34.976
DM: So that gives you disadvantage on ability checks.

02:58:36.436 --> 02:58:36.716
Unknown: Um,

02:58:40.036 --> 02:58:41.156
DM: not Delwath.

02:58:41.156 --> 02:58:42.856
Delwath: No, I... Yeah, I was just playing.

02:58:42.856 --> 02:58:44.556
Delwath: I was just seeing what it did.

02:58:44.556 --> 02:58:45.366
Unknown: [laughs]

02:58:45.366 --> 02:58:45.546
Unknown: Okay. Um,

02:58:46.936 --> 02:58:50.936
DM: so it gives you disadvantage on ability checks until you t- until you get to sleep.

02:58:54.196 --> 02:58:55.836
Seeker: Oh, do I have to do something?

02:58:55.836 --> 02:58:56.506
Seeker: Sorry.

02:58:56.506 --> 02:58:56.606
Unknown: Uh, if-

02:58:56.606 --> 02:58:59.876
Delwath: If you click on your character sheet under conditions.

02:58:59.876 --> 02:59:01.016
Delwath: Do you see where it says conditions?

02:59:01.016 --> 02:59:01.246
Unknown: You can-

02:59:01.246 --> 02:59:04.956
Delwath: You can scroll down, you go to exhausted, and you can click on level one.

02:59:04.956 --> 02:59:05.156
Unknown: Right.

02:59:06.276 --> 02:59:07.396
Seeker: Conditions.

02:59:09.396 --> 02:59:09.955
Delwath: It's like-

02:59:09.956 --> 02:59:10.126
Unknown: Exhausted. Got it

02:59:10.126 --> 02:59:12.636
Delwath: ... next to defenses below your hit points.

02:59:12.636 --> 02:59:13.696
DM: Oh, yeah, yeah. I'm seeing it now.

02:59:16.076 --> 02:59:16.896
Seeker: Got it.

02:59:16.896 --> 02:59:18.276
Seeker: Level one.

02:59:18.276 --> 02:59:19.376
Seeker: Yeah.

02:59:19.376 --> 02:59:19.616
Unknown: Okay.

02:59:21.096 --> 02:59:21.456
Unknown: So

02:59:22.636 --> 02:59:25.296
DM: you get close to the oasis,

02:59:26.676 --> 02:59:30.156
DM: see in the moonlight, um, the

02:59:32.216 --> 02:59:32.756
DM: tents,

02:59:34.336 --> 02:59:38.556
DM: and the quiet scene, palm trees swaying.

02:59:40.536 --> 02:59:44.396
DM: A few, um, y- you hear the flapping in the breeze

02:59:45.696 --> 02:59:50.996
DM: of the tents in f- of the, um, tents and the camp in front of you.

02:59:50.996 --> 02:59:53.236
DM: There's no fire. It seems to be quiet,

02:59:54.596 --> 02:59:55.876
DM: until you look around

02:59:57.076 --> 02:59:57.676
DM: and you see-

02:59:57.676 --> 02:59:59.036
Seeker: They're all dead

02:59:59.036 --> 03:00:00.636
DM: ... in front of you, um-

03:00:02.336 --> 03:00:02.596
Unknown: Mm-mm

03:00:02.596 --> 03:00:03.976
DM: ... dead sheep.

03:00:03.976 --> 03:00:05.356
Wellby: We turn around real quick.

03:00:05.356 --> 03:00:05.896
Unknown: [laughs]

03:00:05.896 --> 03:00:07.036
DM: Three, four of them.

03:00:08.556 --> 03:00:13.936
DM: And in front of the sheep, like chewing on them in the darkness,

03:00:15.616 --> 03:00:19.076
DM: three enormous lizards.

03:00:20.916 --> 03:00:21.276
Unknown: Lizards?

03:00:21.276 --> 03:00:23.956
DM: About, about the size of a small pony.

03:00:26.236 --> 03:00:26.496
Unknown: Oh.

03:00:26.496 --> 03:00:29.996
DM: Much bigger than what you'd expect a lizard to be.

03:00:29.996 --> 03:00:30.256
Unknown: Um,

03:00:33.236 --> 03:00:36.496
DM: tearing into these things, seemingly unaware of your presence.

03:00:38.356 --> 03:00:39.575
DM: And that's where we're gonna stop.

03:00:43.296 --> 03:00:44.776
Seeker: Oh, snap.

03:00:44.776 --> 03:00:45.306
DM: Mm.

03:00:45.306 --> 03:00:45.506
Unknown: Ta-da.

03:00:46.916 --> 03:00:48.356
Kenzo: Uh, all right.

03:00:50.816 --> 03:00:52.016
Seeker: Mm.

03:00:52.016 --> 03:00:54.016
DM: Mm. Giant lizards.

03:00:55.206 --> 03:00:55.236
Unknown: Exciting.

03:00:55.236 --> 03:00:56.436
DM: Pretty, pretty good.

03:00:59.136 --> 03:00:59.816
Unknown: [laughs]

03:00:59.816 --> 03:01:01.076
Kenzo: That was awesome.

03:01:01.076 --> 03:01:03.216
Kenzo: Yeah, that was fun. Totally.

03:01:03.216 --> 03:01:03.246
Unknown: Yeah. [laughs]

03:01:03.246 --> 03:01:03.276
Unknown: [laughs]

03:01:03.276 --> 03:01:05.496
Seeker: Nice to meet everybody's characters and everything, yeah.

03:01:05.496 --> 03:01:06.076
DM: Yeah.

03:01:06.076 --> 03:01:09.056
Seeker: Feel like there's a lot more to unpack here, this is great.

03:01:09.056 --> 03:01:09.236
Unknown: Um-

03:01:09.236 --> 03:01:10.436
Delwath: Totally.

03:01:10.436 --> 03:01:11.876
Kenzo: Mike and Tim?

03:01:11.876 --> 03:01:12.086
Unknown: Yeah?

03:01:12.086 --> 03:01:13.956
Kenzo: Can we, can we stay for, like, five minutes-

03:01:13.956 --> 03:01:14.106
Unknown: Yeah

03:01:14.106 --> 03:01:15.776
Kenzo: ... and finish the conversation that we're having?

